<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand I of Romania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1865–1927</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, of the Hohenzollern-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigmaringen">Sigmaringen</a> family, succeeded his uncle Carol I in 1914. He took Romania into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> on the Allied side in 1916, against his family's sympathies. Victory brought the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukovina">Bukovina</a> with Romania, and he was crowned king of Greater Romania in 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-romania.jpg" alt="Ferdinand I of Romania" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ferdinand_of_Romania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
